        "titulo": "Pocket summary",
        "explicacao": "STEP 1: • 1. Russian has no articles. The last letter decides the gender. STEP 2: • 2. There are three genders: masculine, feminine and neuter. STEP 3: • 3. The general rule: STEP 4: Consonant or -й → masculine STEP 5: -а or -я → feminine STEP 6: -о, -е or -мя → neuter STEP 7: -ь → dictionary STEP 8: • 4. Traps: STEP 9: -ь is ambiguous (dictionary) STEP 10: -мя is always neuter (about 10 words) STEP 11: кофе is masculine (the famous exception) STEP 12: -а/-я words that name males are masculine (папа, дядя, дедушка) STEP 13: дитя is the only neuter word that names a person STEP 14: Loanwords in -и, -у, -ю are neuter (такси, меню) STEP 15: • 5. English gives no clue about gender: a thing is just «it». In Russian the gender belongs to the word, so read the ending. STEP 16: • 6. The English «it» hides a gender. Words like book, car, map, newspaper, problem, name, time, wine, sea, word, milk, tree, health, happiness all have a gender in Russian (some feminine, some neuter, some masculine). Learn them. STEP 17: • 7. Memorise every new word together with its gender. Always. «m», «f» or «n» next to it.",
